---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = 'July 23, 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — FreeSense"
  description="How freesense.org handles your data: no tracking, no advertising cookies, minimal essential storage."
>
  <section class="priv">
    <div class="wrap priv-wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p class="lede">
        FreeSense respects your privacy. <strong>freesense.org</strong> is a static website with no
        user accounts, no advertising, and no cross-site tracking. This page explains the little data
        that is involved when you visit.
      </p>

      <div class="tldr">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>✓ No advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
          <li>✓ No analytics that profile you across sites.</li>
          <li>✓ The only browser storage is your own cookie-consent choice.</li>
          <li>✓ The installed firewall sends no telemetry, device ID, or configuration to us.</li>
          <li>✓ We never sell or share personal data — we don't collect any to begin with.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This site is operated by <strong>The FreeSense Project</strong>, an open-source community
        project. For privacy questions, contact us via the
        <a href="https://github.com/FreeSense-org" rel="noopener">FreeSense-org GitHub organization</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Cookies &amp; local storage</h2>
      <p>
        We do not use cookies for advertising or tracking. The site stores a single value in your
        browser's <code>localStorage</code>, <code>fs-cookie-consent</code>, which simply records
        whether you accepted or declined this notice so we don't ask again. It contains no personal
        information and is never sent to a server. You can clear it any time via your browser
        settings.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Server logs (hosting)</h2>
      <p>
        The website, package service, and download images are served by <strong>Cloudflare</strong>
        (Pages and R2). As part of delivering and protecting them, Cloudflare processes standard request metadata
        such as your IP address, browser user-agent, and the page or file requested. This is used
        only for operating the service, security, and abuse prevention, and is handled under
        Cloudflare's own privacy terms. We do not combine it with anything else or use it to identify
        you.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Third-party requests</h2>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>
          <strong>Google Fonts</strong> — the site loads the “Space Grotesk” webfont from Google's
          font CDN, which means your browser sends a request (including your IP) to Google for the
          font files. No cookies are set by this request.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Releases and updates</strong> — the website reads public release documents from
          <code>pkg.freesense.org</code>. Installer images are served by
          <code>downloads.freesense.org</code>; update manifests, repository metadata, and packages
          are served by <code>pkg.freesense.org</code>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub</strong> — links to source code and issues take you to github.com, which has
          its own privacy policy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Installed FreeSense systems</h2>
      <p>
        FreeSense contains no project telemetry, device registration, automatic configuration
        upload, or usage reporting. The updater makes unauthenticated HTTPS requests to
        <code>pkg.freesense.org</code> for a signed repository manifest, update notes, repository
        metadata, and packages. The appliance does not contact the marketing website for updates.
        Network services and optional packages you enable may contact the upstream services you
        configure; those connections are separate from FreeSense project telemetry.
      </p>

      <h2>6. What we do not do</h2>
      <p>
        We do not run advertising networks, social-media trackers, session recording, or
        fingerprinting. We do not create user profiles. We do not sell, rent, or share personal data.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        If you are in the EU/EEA or UK, the GDPR gives you rights to access, correct, or erase
        personal data and to object to processing. Because this site does not collect or store
        personal data beyond the transient server logs described above, there is normally nothing to
        retrieve — but you are welcome to contact us with any request or question.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site evolves. Material changes will be reflected by the
        “last updated” date above.
      </p>

      <p class="muted small">FreeSense runs on your own hardware. Its source code and outbound update paths are public and auditable.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .priv { padding: 72px 0; }
  .priv-wrap { max-width: 760px; }
  .priv h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 48px); margin: 14px 0 6px; }
  .updated { color: var(--muted-2); font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 22px; }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 19px); color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 28px; }

  .tldr {
    background: var(--ink-3); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 22px 26px; margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .tldr h2 { margin: 0 0 12px; font-size: 18px; }
  .tldr ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 2px; list-style: none; }
  .tldr li { color: var(--muted); padding: 4px 0; font-size: 15px; }

  .priv h2 { font-size: 21px; margin: 34px 0 10px; }
  .priv p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .priv ul.plain { color: var(--muted); padding-left: 20px; }
  .priv ul.plain li { padding: 6px 0; font-size: 15.5px; }
  .small { font-size: 13px; margin-top: 26px; }
</style>
